 "reason": "Every clause of the idea is present and unaltered. Graph side: symmetric count adjacency over the n_train items with zero diagonal; D = ceil(mean degree over all n_train items, isolated counted at 0); N(i) = top-D by count with ascending-id ties; sim_ij = |N(i) cap N(j)|/sqrt(deg_i deg_j) <= 1; coh_i = (1/deg_i) sum_{j in N(i)} sim_ij <= 1 (the truncated-neighbourhood / full-degree scaling is the idea's, and the spec declares the resulting deg^(-3/2) factor rather than hiding it); rho_i = (#{coh_j<coh_i} + 0.5#{coh_j=coh_i, j<i})/(|P|-1) with the item excluded from its own counts, so the support is [0,1], the unique top reaches 1 and a g-way top tie reaches (|P|-1-0.5(g-1))/(|P|-1) — the spec's own statement is arithmetically correct; edge-less items get 0.5 and take no part in the counts. Cost: C_ik = d_c(x_i,y_k) - beta*R_c*(1-|rho_i-s_k|) with c=1, R_c=1, x=exp_0^c(r), y=exp_0^c(a); the offset is maximal (cost minimal) at a matching stratum, so the sign is right, and O in [0,m] with beta=m/R_c so R_c cancels and C and O carry the same (distance) units. m is the median of the distance to the plan's chosen codeword measured in a beta=0 pass at epoch 0 step 0 over the global step-0 batch (the four ranks' 1023-item first batches pooled, 4092 distances) and frozen — the same quantity the idea asks for, not a new estimator. The cost is handed to the baseline's Sinkhorn, which exponentiates it itself exactly once, with the baseline's epsilon, iteration count and marginals (row sums 1, column sums B/K1); k1 = argmax of the plan with ties to the smallest index. STE: p_i = one_hot(k1_i) + P_i - stop_grad(P_i), forward value exactly the raw codeword a_{k1}, and dL/dP_ik = a_k so the gradient passes plan -> C -> |rho_i - s_k| -> sigmoid(alpha_k), training the strata, and reaches the codebook and encoder through d_c; the reconstruction and r_next = r - a_{k1} use the unlifted codeword; levels 2 and 3 stay Euclidean; loss is baseline recon + commit with no new term and no new optimiser. Geometry is consistent across the symbolic surface, the prose and the executable: the Mobius sum substitutes X=-x so the 2c<x,y> terms are negated, denominator 1-2c<x,y>+c^2||x||^2||y||^2, dist = (2/sqrt c) artanh(sqrt c ||(-x)(+)y||) with the 1-1e-6 clamp, lift = tanh(sqrt c ||v||) v/(sqrt c ||v||) = exp_0^c, so d_c(0,lift(v)) = 2||v|| and d_c(x,x)=0; the c->0 limit 2||x-y|| used by GEOMETRY_OFF is the correct limit. Switches do what they claim: BEHAVIOUR_OFF gives C = d_c only while keeping curvature, balancing and strata; GEOMETRY_OFF gives c=0, identity lift, cost 2||u-q|| and the same frozen R_c=1 and frozen beta, i.e. the same-capacity Euclidean control. All tensors are dimensionally consistent (D_k, O_ik, C_ik, P_ik: B x K1; k1, rho_i: B; s_k, alpha_k: K1) and the executable's broadcasting matches. No change of the idea, no missing computation, no wrong sign, scale or limit, and the gradient path is stated for the index, the stratum parameters and the frozen quantities."
